<title>UK: Dowding &amp; Mills full-year profits up 31 pct.</title>
<headline>Dowding &amp; Mills full-year profits up 31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		4.87		   vs 3.77</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.96		   vs 2.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     12.3		   vs 9.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   120		    vs 102</p>
<p>NOTE - Dowding &amp; Mills is involved in electrical and mechanical services. It said in a statement that at the start of its new financial year trading had continued to improve in its main markets. &quot;It this trend continues, then our propsects for the coming year are good,&quot; it said.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 13.06		  vs 9.95</p>
<p> Interest		   0.80		   vs 0.59</p>
<p> Tax			  4.58		   vs 3.60</p>
<p> Net taxed		  7.67		   vs 5.76</p>
<p> Retained profit	  2.83		   vs 1.50</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 31</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 1</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 23</p>
<p>Note - Dowding &amp; Mills Plc chairman Jim Cole said trading had continued to improve in the company's main markets at the start of the new financial year.</p>
<p>&quot;If this trend continues, then our prospects for the coming year are good,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
